From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_fs: do not touch the kiocb after
 aio_complete()

ffs_user_copy_worker() (added by 3adb350 "usb: gadget: f_fs: backport AIO
support for FunctionFS endpoints") calls aio_complete() and then clears
io_data->kiocb->private. In this tree aio_complete() ends with
aio_put_req(), which for a request whose io_submit() has returned drops
the last reference and frees the kiocb. The store therefore writes a NULL
pointer into freed memory, at offset 0x28 of the object (32-bit ARM EABI:
ki_users 0, ki_filp 4, ki_ctx 8, ki_cancel 12, ki_dtor 16, ki_obj 20,
ki_user_data 24, ki_pos 32, private 40).

struct kiocb is 96 bytes and its cache is created with
SLAB_HWCACHE_ALIGN, so with SLUB (no SLUB_DEBUG) it shares slabs with
kmalloc-128. Whatever is allocated from kmalloc-128 between the free and
the store gets its word at 0x28 zeroed. adbd issues one AIO request per
packet, so a logcat stream over adb performs this store thousands of
times a minute.

Seen on gts210ltexx (2026-11-06): three panics in twelve minutes while
logcat was streamed over adb, each consistent with that word being
cleared in a kmalloc-128 object:
- twice "Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference" in
  sync_fence_wait() called from s3c_fb_update_regs(): struct sync_fence
  has pt_list_head.next at 0x28, and the register dump shows the fence
  ("mali_fence", kref 1) intact except pt_list_head = { NULL, <pt> };
- once "kernel BUG at drivers/android/binder.c:4301"
  (BUG_ON(t->buffer == NULL) in binder_thread_read()): struct
  binder_transaction has buffer at 0x28.

Clear the pointer before completing the request.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_fs.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_fs.c
@@ -827,11 +827,15 @@
 		unuse_mm(io_data->mm);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * aio_complete() drops what is normally the last reference to the
+	 * kiocb, so it must not be touched afterwards.
+	 */
+	io_data->kiocb->private = NULL;
 	aio_complete(io_data->kiocb, ret, ret);
 
 	usb_ep_free_request(io_data->ep, io_data->req);
 
-	io_data->kiocb->private = NULL;
 	if (io_data->read)
 		kfree(io_data->iovec);
 	kfree(io_data->buf);
